From 0cc707db0f1acc2fbf5bc187043e28e74d82d3b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 13:47:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 003/638] base: implement native AROS runtime services
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-base-runtime

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: Chromium base selected POSIX implementations that depend on mmap, Unix-domain sockets, dlopen, Linux process handles, signal-stack profilers, and process-private shared memory contracts that AROS does not provide in those forms.

FIX_REASON: Supply capability-specific AROS implementations for files, logging through debug.library, stack symbols, entropy, clocks, synchronization, process/task identity, metrics, and refcounted same-address-space shared regions. Unsupported process launch and Unix-domain transport remain explicit rather than being faked.

SCOPE: base runtime source selection plus AROS files, process, threading, profiler, debug, socket-library, shared-region, metrics, and smoke-probe implementations.

VALIDATION: the native base_runtime_probe passed random, shared-region duplication, synchronization, UTC conversion, and debug.library stack symbolization under SMP QEMU; serial evidence is recorded by ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap.

RISK: medium; shared regions are valid within the current single address space but are not yet OPAL/MMU-enforced cross-domain mappings.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
